productivity inspire</td>\n","      <td>Learn more now</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>595</th>\n","      <td>0.7</td>\n","      <td>tech startup</td>\n","      <td>professional and trustworthy</td>\n","      <td>before and after</td>\n","      <td>feed post</td>\n","      <td>Before and after: Our tech revolution 🚀</td>\n","      <td>tech beforeandafter innovation startup</td>\n","      <td>Join our journey</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["     score     business_type                   brand_voice          occasion  \\\n","252    0.7          wine bar  professional and trustworthy  before and after   \n","279    0.7  co-working space  professional and trustworthy  before and after   \n","595    0.7      tech startup  professional and trustworthy  before and after   \n","\n","        format                                      caption_clean  \\\n","252  feed post            Transform your night with our wines! 🍷🎉   \n","279  feed post  Transform your workspace with us. Before & aft...   \n","595  feed post            Before and after: Our tech revolution 🚀   \n","\n","                                hashtags_clean         cta_clean  \n","252      winebar winelove wineflavors nightcap         Visit us!  \n","279  workspace co_working productivity inspire    Learn more now  \n","595     tech beforeandafter innovation startup  Join our journey  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 13B - RETRIEVE RELEVANT MARKETING EXAMPLES FROM DATASET 5\n","# PURPOSE : Pick the 3 most relevant example posts instead of sending the whole dataset to the LLM.\n","# HOW     : brief_to_query() converts the brief into the query format used by our retriever (Cell 10):\n","#             - free text  = business + service + target customer + goal + location  (TF-IDF text similarity)\n","#             - exact fields = voice, occasion, format, palette (lower-cased; dropped if the dataset doesn't know them)\n","# NOTE    : `platform` is not used for matching because every Dataset 5 example is Instagram.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","def brief_to_query(brief):\n","    text = \" \".join(str(brief.get(k, \"\")) for k in [\"business_type\", \"service\", \"target_customer\", \"marketing_goal\", \"location\"])\n","    query = {\"business_text\": text}\n","    for brief_key, lib_col in BRIEF_TO_LIB.items():\n","        value = str(brief.get(brief_key, \"\")).strip().lower()      # dataset values are lowercase\n","        if value in VOCAB[lib_col]:                                  # only use values the dataset really contains\n","            query[lib_col] = value\n","    return query\n","\n","query_used = brief_to_query(marketing_brief)\n","print(\"Query sent to the retriever:\"); print(json.dumps(query_used, indent=2))\n","retrieved_examples = retrieve_examples(query_used, k=3)\n","print(\"\\nRetrieved examples:\")\n","display(retrieved_examples[[\"score\", \"business_type\", \"brand_voice\", \"occasion\", \"format\", \"caption_clean\", \"hashtags_clean\", \"cta_clean\"]])"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":16,"id":"bc6f0dd9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.767808Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.767495Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.778478Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.777299Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.02537,"end_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.781144+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.755774+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["LLM prompt created successfully.\n","================================================================================\n","You are an AI marketing content assistant.\n","Create social-media marketing content for a business using the information below.\n","\n","IMPORTANT RULES:\n","1. The TARGET CUSTOMER must strongly influence the hashtags, caption, CTA and content idea.\n","2. The SERVICE must be clearly relevant to the generated content.\n","3. The PLATFORM (Instagram) must influence the writing style and hashtag selection. Short, punchy caption (about 8-40 words). Emojis allowed in moderation. Hashtags go ONLY in the hashtags field.\n","4. The MARKETING GOAL must influence the CTA.\n","5. The LOCATION may be used in hashtags when it is relevant.\n","6. Use ONLY facts from the business information. Do not invent prices, discounts, awards, certifications, statistics, guarantees, project results or customer reviews.\n","7. Do not copy the retrieved examples. They come from other businesses and are only style references.\n","8. Generate 5 to 10 relevant hashtags, each starting with '#', no spaces, no duplicates.\n","9. Hashtags must relate to the target customer, service, platform, goal, or location. Do not add random trending or engagement-bait hashtags.\n","10. No '#' symbols inside the caption.\n","11. Return ONLY valid JSON.\n","\n","BUSINESS INFORMATION:\n","Business Type: Civil Works Company\n","Service: Bathroom Renovation\n","Target Customer: Homeowners\n","Platform: Instagram\n","Marketing Goal: Generate Enquiries\n","Brand Voice: Professional and Trustworthy\n","Location: Chennai\n","Content Format: Feed Post\n","Occasion: Before and After\n","Brand Palette: Muted Neutrals\n","\n","RETRIEVED MARKETING EXAMPLES (style only):\n","\n","--- Example 1 (style reference from ANOTHER business) ---\n","Business Type: wine bar\n","Brand Voice: professional and trustworthy\n","Format: feed post\n","Occasion: before and after\n","Caption: Transform your night with our wines! 🍷🎉\n","Hashtags: winebar winelove wineflavors nightcap\n","CTA: Visit us!\n","Image prompt: A wine bar with a selection of vibrant, ocean-colored wine bottles and a glass of wine on the table\n","\n","--- Example 2 (style reference from ANOTHER business) ---\n","Business Type: co-working space\n","Brand Voice: professional and trustworthy\n","Format: feed post\n","Occasion: before and after\n","Caption: Transform your workspace with us. Before & after, you'll see a difference.\n","Hashtags: workspace co_working productivity inspire\n","CTA: Learn more now\n","Image prompt: Before and after view of a professional co-working space, contrasting old and new\n","\n","--- Example 3 (style reference from ANOTHER business) ---\n","Business Type: tech startup\n","Brand Voice: professional and trustworthy\n","Format: feed post\n","Occasion: before and after\n","Caption: Before and after: Our tech revolution 🚀\n","Hashtags: tech beforeandafter innovation startup\n","CTA: Join our journey\n","Image prompt: A row of black and white tech gadgets, one with vibrant colors\n","\n","REQUIRED OUTPUT (JSON):\n","{\n","  \"caption\": \"Social media caption\",\n","  \"hashtags\": [\"#hashtag1\", \"#hashtag2\", \"#hashtag3\", \"#hashtag4\", \"#hashtag5\"],\n","  \"cta\": \"One clear call to action\",\n","  \"content_idea\": \"One content idea\",\n","  \"image_prompt\": \"Realistic image generation prompt\"\n","}\n","\n"]}],"source":["# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 13C - BUILD THE TARGET-CUSTOMER-AWARE LLM PROMPT\n","# PURPOSE : Combine the user's brief and the retrieved examples into one instruction for any LLM.\n","# KEY IDEA: The prompt tells the LLM that TARGET CUSTOMER, SERVICE, PLATFORM, GOAL and LOCATION must shape the\n","#           caption, hashtags and CTA, while the retrieved examples are used ONLY for style (not copied).\n","# HASHTAG COUNT depends on the platform (Instagram 5-10, Facebook/LinkedIn 1-3), defined once in HASHTAG_LIMITS and reused by the validator.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","HASHTAG_LIMITS = {\"Instagram\": (5, 10), \"Facebook\": (1, 3), \"LinkedIn\": (1, 3)}    # (minimum, maximum)\n","PLATFORM_RULES = {\n","    \"Instagram\": \"Short, punchy caption (about 8-40 words). Emojis allowed in moderation. Hashtags go ONLY in the hashtags field.\",\n","    \"Facebook\":  \"Conversational caption of 1-3 sentences.\",\n","    \"LinkedIn\":  \"Professional caption of 2-4 sentences, minimal emojis.\",\n","}\n","\n","def build_llm_prompt(brief, examples_df):\n","    platform = brief.get(\"platform\", \"Instagram\")\n","    lo, hi = HASHTAG_LIMITS.get(platform, (3, 8))\n","    # One text block per retrieved example (iterrows gives the rows; looping over the DataFrame directly would give column names)\n","    examples_text = \"\"\n","    for i, (_, ex) in enumerate(examples_df.iterrows(), start=1):\n","        examples_text += (f\"\\n--- Example {i} (style reference from ANOTHER business) ---\\n\"\n","                          f\"Business Type: {ex['business_type']}\\nBrand Voice: {ex['brand_voice']}\\nFormat: {ex['format']}\\n\"\n","                          f\"Occasion: {ex['occasion']}\\nCaption: {ex['caption_clean']}\\nHashtags: {ex['hashtags_clean']}\\n\"\n","                          f\"CTA: {ex['cta_clean']}\\nImage prompt: {ex['image_prompt']}\\n\")\n","    return f\"\"\"You are an AI marketing content assistant.\n","Create social-media marketing content for a business using the information below.\n","\n","IMPORTANT RULES:\n","1. The TARGET CUSTOMER must strongly influence the hashtags, caption, CTA and content idea.\n","2. The SERVICE must be clearly relevant to the generated content.\n","3. The PLATFORM ({platform}) must influence the writing style and hashtag selection. {PLATFORM_RULES.get(platform, \"\")}\n","4. The MARKETING GOAL must influence the CTA.\n","5. The LOCATION may be used in hashtags when it is relevant.\n","6. Use ONLY facts from the business information. Do not invent prices, discounts, awards, certifications, statistics, guarantees, project results or customer reviews.\n","7. Do not copy the retrieved examples. They come from other businesses and are only style references.\n","8. Generate {lo} to {hi} relevant hashtags, each starting with '#', no spaces, no duplicates.\n","9. Hashtags must relate to the target customer, service, platform, goal, or location. Do not add random trending or engagement-bait hashtags.\n","10. No '#' symbols inside the caption.\n","11. Return ONLY valid JSON.\n","\n","BUSINESS INFORMATION:\n","Business Type: {brief.get(\"business_type\", \"\")}\n","Service: {brief.get(\"service\", \"\")}\n","Target Customer: {brief.get(\"target_customer\", \"\")}\n","Platform: {platform}\n","Marketing Goal: {brief.get(\"marketing_goal\", \"\")}\n","Brand Voice: {brief.get(\"brand_voice\", \"\")}\n","Location: {brief.get(\"location\", \"\")}\n","Content Format: {brief.get(\"content_format\", \"\")}\n","Occasion: {brief.get(\"occasion\", \"\")}\n","Brand Palette: {brief.get(\"brand_palette\", \"\")}\n","\n","RETRIEVED MARKETING EXAMPLES (style only):\n","{examples_text}\n","REQUIRED OUTPUT (JSON):\n","{{\n","  \"caption\": \"Social media caption\",\n","  \"hashtags\": [\"#hashtag1\", \"#hashtag2\", \"#hashtag3\", \"#hashtag4\", \"#hashtag5\"],\n","  \"cta\": \"One clear call to action\",\n","  \"content_idea\": \"One content idea\",\n","  \"image_prompt\": \"Realistic image generation prompt\"\n","}}\n","\"\"\"\n","\n","llm_prompt = build_llm_prompt(marketing_brief, retrieved_examples)\n","print(\"LLM prompt created successfully.\")\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","print(llm_prompt)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":17,"id":"f1fb5f7c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.803782Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.803442Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.82097Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.819961Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.031467,"end_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.822943+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.791476+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["=== Brief 1 (civil works / homeowners) ===\n","OK business_type: Civil Works Company\n","OK service: Bathroom Renovation\n","OK target_customer: Homeowners\n","OK platform: Instagram\n","OK marketing_goal: Generate Enquiries\n","OK brand_voice: Professional and Trustworthy\n","OK location: Chennai\n","\n","=== Brief 2 (commercial construction / property developers) ===\n","OK business_type: Civil Works Company\n","OK service: Commercial Construction\n","OK target_customer: Property Developers\n","OK platform: Instagram\n","OK marketing_goal: Generate Enquiries\n","OK brand_voice: Professional and Trustworthy\n","OK location: Chennai\n","\n","Business-information lines that changed between the two prompts (driven by the user's input):\n","  > Service: Commercial Construction\n","  > Target Customer: Property Developers\n","  > Occasion: Behind the Scenes\n","\n","All required fields reached both prompts: True\n"]}],"source":["# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 13D - CHECK THAT THE USER'S INFORMATION REACHES THE PROMPT\n","# PURPOSE : Before spending any LLM/API call, confirm every important brief field is present in the prompt text.\n","# ALSO    : Builds a SECOND, different brief (property developers) to show the prompt changes with the target customer.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","required_fields = [\"business_type\", \"service\", \"target_customer\", \"platform\", \"marketing_goal\", \"brand_voice\", \"location\"]\n","\n","def check_prompt_inputs(brief, prompt):\n","    all_ok = True\n","    for field in required_fields:\n","        value = brief.get(field)\n","        if not value:\n","            print(f\"X Missing in brief: {field}\"); all_ok = False\n","        elif str(value) not in prompt:\n","            print(f\"X In brief but NOT in prompt: {field} = {value}\"); all_ok = False\n","        else:\n","            print(f\"OK {field}: {value}\")\n","    return all_ok\n","\n","print(\"=== Brief 1 (civil works / homeowners) ===\")\n","ok1 = check_prompt_inputs(marketing_brief, llm_prompt)\n","\n","brief_2 = {\"business_type\": \"Civil Works Company\", \"service\": \"Commercial Construction\", \"target_customer\": \"Property Developers\",\n","           \"platform\": \"Instagram\", \"marketing_goal\": \"Generate Enquiries\", \"brand_voice\": \"Professional and Trustworthy\",\n","           \"location\": \"Chennai\", \"content_format\": \"Feed Post\", \"occasion\": \"Behind the Scenes\", \"brand_palette\": \"Muted Neutrals\"}\n","prompt_2 = build_llm_prompt(brief_2, retrieve_examples(brief_to_query(brief_2), k=3))\n","print(\"\\n=== Brief 2 (commercial construction / property developers) ===\")\n","ok2 = check_prompt_inputs(brief_2, prompt_2)\n","\n","def business_info_lines(prompt):\n","    \"\"\"Only the 'BUSINESS INFORMATION' block of a prompt (what the user typed), without the example posts.\"\"\"\n","    block = prompt.split(\"BUSINESS INFORMATION:\")[1].split(\"RETRIEVED MARKETING EXAMPLES\")[0]\n","    return [l.strip() for l in block.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n","\n","changed = [l for l in business_info_lines(prompt_2) if l not in business_info_lines(llm_prompt)]\n","print(\"\\nBusiness-information lines that changed between the two prompts (driven by the user's input):\")\n","for l in changed: print(\"  >\", l)\n","print(\"\\nAll required fields reached both prompts:\", ok1 and ok2)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"id":"6ff4e6ab","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.845497Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.845159Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.865259Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.864285Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.033727,"end_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.867117+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.83339+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Validators ready: validate_hashtags, validate_content, parse_llm_json\n"]}],"source":["# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 14 - VALIDATORS (hashtags + the whole generated post) AND JSON PARSER\n","# PURPOSE : Catch mechanical mistakes in the LLM output automatically, before human approval.\n","# WHAT IT CHECKS (format, count, duplicates, rules) - it does NOT judge whether a hashtag is semantically relevant.\n","#           Relevance (\"#DreamHome\" fits homeowners) is a human judgement, so it stays in the Human Approval step.\n","# HASHTAGS: must be a list, within the platform's min-max count, each written '#word' (no spaces), no duplicates,\n","#           and not engagement-bait such as #followforfollow.\n","# POST    : also checks required JSON keys, caption length, no '#' inside the caption, a CTA, image prompt, content idea,\n","#           possible invented claims (guarantee, 100%, free, prices...) and copying from the library.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","SPAM_HASHTAGS = {\"followforfollow\", \"follow4follow\", \"f4f\", \"like4like\", \"likeforlike\", \"l4l\", \"followback\", \"tagsforlikes\", \"likesforlikes\"}\n","REQUIRED_KEYS = [\"caption\", \"hashtags\", \"cta\", \"content_idea\", \"image_prompt\"]\n","CLAIM_PATTERNS = [r\"\\bguarantee[sd]?\\b\", r\"\\b100\\s?%\", r\"\\b#?1\\b.*\\b(best|rated|choice)\\b\", r\"\\bbest\\b.*\\b(in|of)\\b\",\n","                  r\"\\bfree\\b\", r\"\\$\\s?\\d\", r\"\\b\\d+\\s?%\\s?off\\b\", r\"\\baward\", r\"\\bsince\\s+\\d{4}\\b\", r\"\\bcertified\\b\"]\n","\n","def validate_hashtags(hashtags, target_customer=None, service=None, platform=\"Instagram\", min_count=None, max_count=None):\n","    \"\"\"Return a list of problems (empty list = passed).\n","    target_customer and service are accepted so the call matches the project spec, but they are NOT used to reject hashtags.\"\"\"\n","    issues = []\n","    if not isinstance(hashtags, list):\n","        return [\"Hashtags must be returned as a list.\"]\n","    lo, hi = HASHTAG_LIMITS.get(platform, (3, 8))\n","    lo = lo if min_count is None else min_count\n","    hi = hi if max_count is None else max_count\n","    if len(hashtags) < lo: issues.append(f\"Too few hashtags ({len(hashtags)}; need at least {lo}).\")\n","    if len(hashtags) > hi: issues.append(f\"Too many hashtags ({len(hashtags)}; at most {hi}).\")\n","    cleaned = []\n","    for tag in hashtags:\n","        if not isinstance(tag, str):\n","            issues.append(\"A hashtag is not a string.\"); continue\n","        tag = tag.strip()\n","        if not re.fullmatch(r\"#\\w+\", tag):                    # '#' followed by letters/digits/underscore only\n","            issues.append(f\"Invalid hashtag format: '{tag}'\")\n","        if tag.lstrip(\"#\").lower() in SPAM_HASHTAGS:\n","            issues.append(f\"Engagement-bait hashtag: '{tag}'\")\n","        cleaned.append(tag.lower())\n","    if len(cleaned) != len(set(cleaned)):\n","        issues.append(\"Duplicate hashtags found.\")\n","    return issues\n","\n","def jaccard(a, b):                    # word-overlap similarity between two texts (0 = nothing shared, 1 = identical)\n","    a, b = set(a.lower().split()), set(b.lower().split())\n","    return len(a & b) / max(1, len(a | b))\n","\n","def validate_content(c, brief=None, platform=\"Instagram\", allowed_claims=(), library_df=None, min_tags=None, max_tags=None):\n","    problems, warnings_ = [], []                       # problems = must fix | warnings = a human should look\n","    for key in REQUIRED_KEYS:\n","        if key not in c: problems.append(f\"missing key: {key}\")\n","    cap  = str(c.get(\"caption\", \"\")).strip()\n","    cta  = str(c.get(\"cta\", \"\")).strip()\n","    img  = str(c.get(\"image_prompt\", \"\")).strip()\n","    idea = str(c.get(\"content_idea\", \"\")).strip()\n","    tags = c.get(\"hashtags\", [])\n","    if isinstance(tags, str): tags = tags.split()      # raw dataset rows store hashtags as one string\n","    tp = (brief or {}).get(\"target_customer\"); sv = (brief or {}).get(\"service\")\n","    problems += validate_hashtags(tags, tp, sv, platform, min_tags, max_tags)\n","\n","    if not cap: problems.append(\"caption is empty\")\n","    elif len(cap.split()) < 4: problems.append(\"caption shorter than 4 words\")\n","    elif len(cap.split()) > 60: problems.append(\"caption longer than 60 words\")\n","    if \"#\" in cap: problems.append(\"caption contains '#' (hashtags belong in the hashtags field)\")\n","    if not cta: problems.append(\"no call-to-action\")\n","    elif len(cta.split()) > 8: problems.append(\"CTA longer than 8 words\")\n","    if len(img.split()) < 5: problems.append(\"image_prompt missing or too short\")\n","    if \"content_idea\" in c and len(idea.split()) < 3: problems.append(\"content_idea missing or too short\")\n","\n","    text_all = (cap + \" \" + cta).lower()\n","    for pat in CLAIM_PATTERNS:                         # claims the brief did not allow -> warn the human\n","        m = re.search(pat, text_all)\n","        if m and not any(a.lower() in text_all for a in allowed_claims):\n","            warnings_.append(f\"unsupported claim? '{m.group(0)}' - not in the brief, needs human check\")\n","    if library_df is not None and cap:                 # is the caption almost a copy of a library caption?\n","        j = float(library_df[\"caption_clean\"].map(lambda x: jaccard(cap, x)).max())\n","        if j > 0.7: warnings_.append(f\"caption is {j:.0%} similar to a library caption (possible copy)\")\n","    return {\"passed\": len(problems) == 0, \"problems\": problems, \"warnings\": warnings_}\n","\n","def parse_llm_json(text):\n","    \"\"\"LLMs sometimes wrap JSON in ```json fences or add a sentence around it. Extract and parse the JSON object.\"\"\"\n","    t = re.sub(r\"^```(?:json)?\\s*|\\s*```$\", \"\", text.strip())\n","    start, end = t.find(\"{\"), t.rfind(\"}\")\n","    if start == -1 or end == -1: raise ValueError(\"no JSON object found in the LLM response\")\n","    return json.loads(t[start:end + 1])\n","print(\"Validators ready: validate_hashtags, validate_content, parse_llm_json\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"id":"1ea9aad4","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.889837Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.889496Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.897043Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.896224Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020962,"end_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.898773+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.877811+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[PASS] good list (6 tags)\n","[FAIL] too few\n","      - Too few hashtags (2; need at least 5).\n","[FAIL] duplicates + no #\n","      - Invalid hashtag format: 'HomeImprovement'\n","      - Duplicate hashtags found.\n","[FAIL] space inside a hashtag\n","      - Invalid hashtag format: '#Bathroom Renovation'\n","[FAIL] engagement bait\n","      - Engagement-bait hashtag: '#followforfollow'\n","[FAIL] not a list\n","      - Hashtags must be returned as a list.\n","\n","Same 6-tag list on LinkedIn (limit 1-3): ['Too many hashtags (6; at most 3).']\n"]}],"source":["# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 14B - TEST THE HASHTAG VALIDATOR\n","# PURPOSE : Prove the validator accepts a good list and catches common mistakes.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","tests = {\n","    \"good list (6 tags)\":      [\"#BathroomRenovation\", \"#HomeRenovation\", \"#HomeImprovement\", \"#BathroomMakeover\", \"#ChennaiHomes\", \"#RenovationIdeas\"],\n","    \"too few\":                 [\"#BathroomRenovation\", \"#HomeRenovation\"],\n","    \"duplicates + no #\":       [\"#BathroomRenovation\", \"#bathroomrenovation\", \"HomeImprovement\", \"#Chennai\", \"#Homes\"],\n","    \"space inside a hashtag\":  [\"#Bathroom Renovation\", \"#HomeRenovation\", \"#HomeImprovement\", \"#Chennai\", \"#Homes\"],\n","    \"engagement bait\":         [\"#BathroomRenovation\", \"#HomeRenovation\", \"#HomeImprovement\", \"#Chennai\", \"#followforfollow\"],\n","    \"not a list\":              \"#BathroomRenovation #HomeRenovation\",\n","}\n","for name, tags in tests.items():\n","    issues = validate_hashtags(tags, target_customer=\"Homeowners\", service=\"Bathroom Renovation\", platform=\"Instagram\")\n","    print(f\"[{'PASS' if not issues else 'FAIL'}] {name}\")\n","    for i in issues: print(\"      -\", i)\n","print(\"\\nSame 6-tag list on LinkedIn (limit 1-3):\", validate_hashtags(tests[\"good list (6 tags)\"], platform=\"LinkedIn\"))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"id":"fbc6c1ca","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.921541Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.921134Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.118837Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.117932Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.211274,"end_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.120656+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:05.909382+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","--- good response ---\n","{\n","  \"passed\": true,\n","  \"problems\": [],\n","  \"warnings\": []\n","}\n","\n","--- bad response ---\n","{\n","  \"passed\": false,\n","  \"problems\": [\n","    \"missing key: content_idea\",\n","    \"missing key: image_prompt\",\n","    \"Too few hashtags (2; need at least 5).\",\n","    \"Duplicate hashtags found.\",\n","    \"caption contains '#' (hashtags belong in the hashtags field)\",\n","    \"no call-to-action\",\n","    \"image_prompt missing or too short\"\n","  ],\n","  \"warnings\": [\n","    \"unsupported claim? 'guaranteed' - not in the brief, needs human check\",\n","    \"unsupported claim? '100%' - not in the brief, needs human check\",\n","    \"unsupported claim? 'best renovation in' - not in the brief, needs human check\"\n","  ]\n","}\n","\n","--- broken (no JSON) response ---\n","Could not parse -> would be sent back to the LLM for a retry. Reason: no JSON object found in the LLM response\n","\n","Dataset audit - pass rate on RAW rows    : 35.7%\n","Dataset audit - pass rate on CLEANED rows: 99.3%\n"]}],"source":["# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 14C - END-TO-END CHECK OF THE OUTPUT PIPELINE (LLM text -> parse -> validate)\n","# PURPOSE : Test parsing and validation of a full response WITHOUT calling a real LLM.\n","# NOTE    : The three responses below are HAND-WRITTEN test inputs, NOT real LLM output.\n","#           In production, `llm_text` would be the string returned by your LLM API.\n","# ALSO    : Audits Dataset 5 itself with the same validator (raw vs cleaned) to show why Cell 8 mattered.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","good_text = '''```json\n","{\"caption\": \"Before and after: a bathroom brought back to life, planned and finished by our team. Message us to start your renovation.\",\n"," \"hashtags\": [\"#BathroomRenovation\", \"#HomeRenovation\", \"#HomeImprovement\", \"#BathroomMakeover\", \"#ChennaiHomes\", \"#RenovationIdeas\"],\n"," \"cta\": \"Message us for a site visit\",\n"," \"content_idea\": \"Side-by-side photos of the old and renovated bathroom\",\n"," \"image_prompt\": \"Realistic before and after photo of a renovated bathroom in muted neutral tones, clean tiles\"}\n","```'''\n","bad_text = '{\"caption\": \"Best renovation in town! 100% guaranteed #reno\", \"hashtags\": [\"#reno\", \"#reno\"], \"cta\": \"\"}'\n","broken_text = \"Sure! Here is your post: caption - great bathrooms\"\n","\n","for name, text in [(\"good\", good_text), (\"bad\", bad_text), (\"broken (no JSON)\", broken_text)]:\n","    print(f\"\\n--- {name} response ---\")\n","    try:\n","        parsed = parse_llm_json(text)\n","        print(json.dumps(validate_content(parsed, brief=marketing_brief, library_df=RET[\"library\"]), indent=2))\n","    except Exception as e:\n","        print(\"Could not parse -> would be sent back to the LLM for a retry. Reason:\", e)\n","\n","# Audit of the dataset itself (library examples carry ~4 hashtags, so the minimum is relaxed to 2 for this audit only)\n","raw_pass = df.apply(lambda r: validate_content({\"caption\": r[\"caption\"], \"hashtags\": r[\"hashtags\"], \"cta\": r[\"cta\"],\n","                    \"image_prompt\": r[\"image_prompt\"], \"content_idea\": \"n/a n/a n/a\"}, min_tags=2, max_tags=10)[\"passed\"], axis=1)\n","clean_pass = df.apply(lambda r: validate_content({\"caption\": r[\"caption_clean\"], \"hashtags\": [\"#\" + t for t in r[\"hashtag_list\"]],\n","                    \"cta\": r[\"cta_clean\"], \"image_prompt\": r[\"image_prompt\"], \"content_idea\": \"n/a n/a n/a\"}, min_tags=2, max_tags=10)[\"passed\"], axis=1)\n","print(f\"\\nDataset audit - pass rate on RAW rows    : {raw_pass.mean():.1%}\")\n","print(f\"Dataset audit - pass rate on CLEANED rows: {clean_pass.mean():.1%}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"015188c2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.14421Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.143823Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.168295Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.167386Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.038722,"end_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.170173+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-07T04:49:06.131451+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["=== How much civil-works content exists in Dataset 5? ===\n"]},{"data":{"text/plain":["civil            0\n","plumb            0\n","waterproof    