,"output                                                                               \n","Caption wording                     LLM, guided by Dataset 5 style examples + the ...\n","Hashtags                            LLM, steered by target customer + service + pl...\n","CTA                                 LLM, steered by the marketing goal (Dataset 5 ...\n","Content idea                             LLM + strategy layer / customer intelligence\n","Image prompt                        LLM + uploaded image + palette (Dataset 5 show...\n","Platform version                    Rules (PLATFORM_RULES, HASHTAG_LIMITS) + forma...\n","Facts (services, location, claims)    ONLY the business's own input - never Dataset 5"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Dataset 5 provides: structure, length, tone and CTA/hashtag style examples. It provides NO civil-works knowledge and NO performance evidence.\n"]}],"source":["## Cell 15: Quality analysis\n","\n","# =====================================================================================\n","# CELL 15 - QUALITY ANALYSIS: WHAT DATASET 5 CAN AND CANNOT PROVIDE\n","# PURPOSE : Count how much civil-works knowledge the dataset really contains, and map each output part to its true source.\n","# KEY FINDING: almost none, so civil-works knowledge must come from the USER's brief. Dataset 5 gives STRUCTURE and STYLE only.\n","# =====================================================================================\n","civil_words = [\"civil\", \"plumb\", \"waterproof\", \"renovat\", \"bathroom\", \"tile\", \"repair\", \"construction\", \"contractor\", \"paint\"]\n","corpus = \" \".join(df[\"doc_text\"])\n","cov = pd.Series({w: len(re.findall(w, corpus)) for w in civil_words}, name=\"mentions in dataset\")\n","print(\"=== How much civil-works content exists in Dataset 5? ===\"); display(cov)\n","\n","print(\"\\n=== What each part of the final output must come from ===\")\n","sources =